risk is a big thing for us.

00:24:27.870 --> 00:24:28.370
Right.

00:24:28.370 --> 00:24:32.810
So what are the biggest risks
in the cloud migration space?

00:24:32.810 --> 00:24:35.520
One of the risks--

00:24:35.520 --> 00:24:38.490
one of the risks is around
not knowing your environment.

00:24:38.490 --> 00:24:41.000
So environment discovery
is super important.

00:24:41.000 --> 00:24:43.397
Very scalable
environment discovery

00:24:43.397 --> 00:24:45.230
helps you get through
thousands of workloads

00:24:45.230 --> 00:24:47.870
in a very short period of
time and, most importantly,

00:24:47.870 --> 00:24:49.310
from there what
it's going to let

00:24:49.310 --> 00:24:52.100
you do is actually map
those workloads globally

00:24:52.100 --> 00:24:52.850
on a global sync.

00:24:52.850 --> 00:24:55.760
If you've got data centers
in multiple locations,

00:24:55.760 --> 00:24:57.750
you've got data centers
in multiple countries,

00:24:57.750 --> 00:24:58.580
it doesn't matter.

00:24:58.580 --> 00:25:00.030
Pull everything together.

00:25:00.030 --> 00:25:02.030
And the other big risk
that customers face today

00:25:02.030 --> 00:25:04.950
is around the requirements.

00:25:04.950 --> 00:25:08.870
Your risks around your
requirements stem from the fact

00:25:08.870 --> 00:25:10.460
that a cloud strategy
has to be based

00:25:10.460 --> 00:25:14.330
on your CFO's priorities, your
organization's priorities,

00:25:14.330 --> 00:25:18.110
and, most importantly,
your best way

00:25:18.110 --> 00:25:22.560
to get the return on investment
from a cloud strategy.

00:25:22.560 --> 00:25:24.840
And when you put those
two things together,

00:25:24.840 --> 00:25:28.100
one of the things that
we do as a platform is

00:25:28.100 --> 00:25:32.180
we're going to get your
consumption velocity moved up.

00:25:32.180 --> 00:25:34.580
And why do you need your
consumption velocity moved up?

00:25:34.580 --> 00:25:35.750
One of the biggest
challenges we've

00:25:35.750 --> 00:25:37.917
seen over thousands and
thousands of workloads being

00:25:37.917 --> 00:25:39.500
moved to the cloud
is that when you're

00:25:39.500 --> 00:25:40.970
straddling both
sides of the fence,

00:25:40.970 --> 00:25:43.310
you're still part
private and you slow down

00:25:43.310 --> 00:25:45.050
in your consumption
into cloud, you

00:25:45.050 --> 00:25:47.990
are going to end up with an
extra cost, because you're

00:25:47.990 --> 00:25:49.000
straddling both sides.

00:25:49.000 --> 00:25:51.020
Your resources have
to be doubled up.

00:25:51.020 --> 00:25:53.090
Your facilities have
to be doubled up.

00:25:53.090 --> 00:25:54.800
You can't exactly shut
down a data center

00:25:54.800 --> 00:25:57.440
so your footprint still remains
out there, power cooling,

00:25:57.440 --> 00:25:58.470
so on and so forth.

00:25:58.470 --> 00:26:00.470
So there's a lot
around the risk factors

00:26:00.470 --> 00:26:02.280
that you have to take
into consideration.

00:26:02.280 --> 00:26:05.960
So our entire goal is to help
you accelerate that consumption

00:26:05.960 --> 00:26:06.740
cycle.

00:26:06.740 --> 00:26:08.480
So most importantly,
