00:26:14.360 --> 00:26:17.660
Once you get that, you can put
a roadmap together very easily.

00:26:17.660 --> 00:26:19.820
The challenge in
getting there is if you

00:26:19.820 --> 00:26:22.410
don't have that roadmap--

00:26:22.410 --> 00:26:24.830
what we call a
consumable roadmap

00:26:24.830 --> 00:26:27.830
has to be realistic
and consumable.

00:26:27.830 --> 00:26:30.830
It's the biggest missing
piece in most customers' cloud

00:26:30.830 --> 00:26:31.430
planning.

00:26:31.430 --> 00:26:33.470
So once you get a
consumable roadmap, that's

00:26:33.470 --> 00:26:34.910
what goes where and when.

00:26:34.910 --> 00:26:36.050
What is the delivery model?

00:26:36.050 --> 00:26:38.090
What am I consuming with
platform as a service?

00:26:38.090 --> 00:26:41.060
What am I consuming with
infrastructure as a service?

00:26:41.060 --> 00:26:42.265
What stays private?

00:26:42.265 --> 00:26:43.390
What can move to the cloud?

00:26:43.390 --> 00:26:43.560
Right.

00:26:43.560 --> 00:26:45.690
So basically, we call
that the delivery model.

00:26:45.690 --> 00:26:48.350
How are you going to deliver
cloud to your organization?

00:26:48.350 --> 00:26:49.970
And the implementation model.

00:26:49.970 --> 00:26:52.610
Are you going to implement
cloud across all your assets

00:26:52.610 --> 00:26:54.680
or are you going to stay with
just a few assets that will end

00:26:54.680 --> 00:26:56.090
up going into the cloud, right?

00:26:56.090 --> 00:26:58.730
So really having a
good grip on that

00:26:58.730 --> 00:27:00.892
is the biggest priority
for most of our customers.

00:27:00.892 --> 00:27:03.350
Now, of course, the platform
will pick for you the best fit

00:27:03.350 --> 00:27:04.220
