a migration runbook that you

00:31:00.790 --> 00:31:04.080
would need in order to get
from point A to point B.

00:31:04.080 --> 00:31:06.420
So how do you get started?

00:31:06.420 --> 00:31:08.055
Again, to a pointer
from earlier,

00:31:08.055 --> 00:31:10.680
Google has licensed the platform
so it's available to customers

00:31:10.680 --> 00:31:12.060
for free.

00:31:12.060 --> 00:31:13.920
You fill up a form.

00:31:13.920 --> 00:31:16.410
The form asks you to tell
us about your data center

00:31:16.410 --> 00:31:17.500
environments.

00:31:17.500 --> 00:31:19.603
Those environments are
important because we'd

00:31:19.603 --> 00:31:21.520
like to know how you
want your data rolled up.

00:31:21.520 --> 00:31:23.460
So once you fill
in that form, it'll

00:31:23.460 --> 00:31:26.640
workflow to you a series
of data collectors

00:31:26.640 --> 00:31:28.320
that are uniquely
numbered and tagged.

00:31:28.320 --> 00:31:29.940
And what those
data collectors do

00:31:29.940 --> 00:31:32.640
is that they report into
the platform with the way

00:31:32.640 --> 00:31:33.850
you want to see your data.

00:31:33.850 --> 00:31:36.743
So it could be EMIA, you know
North America, data center one,

00:31:36.743 --> 00:31:37.410
data center two.

00:31:37.410 --> 00:31:38.160
It doesn't matter.

00:31:38.160 --> 00:31:38.880
We pretag data.

00:31:38.880 --> 00:31:41.220
It's very important for
us, very important for you,

00:31:41.220 --> 00:31:43.700
because the level of
automation gives you reports

00:31:43.700 --> 00:31:44.920
starting the next morning.

00:31:44.920 --> 00:31:45.120
Right.

00:31:45.120 --> 00:31:46.800
You're going to start
seeing reports come in.

00:31:46.800 --> 00:31:49.383
And we'd like to see them tagged
the way you want to see them.

00:31:49.383 --> 00:31:51.575
So 30 minutes to install
a data collector.

00:31:51.575 --> 00:31:53.700
You can start looking at
results in a couple hours.

00:31:53.700 --> 00:31:57.512
We'd like to do at least
one day of data pulls.

00:31:57.512 --> 00:31:59.720
The longer you let it run,
the better the data looks.

00:31:59.720 --> 00:32:00.210
Right.

00:32:00.210 --> 00:32:01.260
And the most
important thing here

00:32:01.260 --> 00:32:03.060
is that, let's say
you're a retailer

00:32:03.060 --> 00:32:04.950
and you have something that
you want to check in November

00:32:04.950 --> 00:32:06.460
or you have an end
of month process.

00:32:06.460 --> 00:32:08.220
You can schedule
the data collectors

00:32:08.220 --> 00:32:11.160
to kick off again at the end of
the month, or end of the week,

00:32:11.160 --> 00:32:14.830
or whenever that anticipated
peak period is going to be.

00:32:14.830 --> 00:32:16.500
So that is the
extent of the work

00:32:16.500 --> 00:32:19.690
you to start doing an
assessment in your environment.

00:32:19.690 --> 00:32:20.190
Right.

00:32:20.190 --> 00:32:21.540
It's 30 minutes per collector.

00:32:21.540 --> 00:32:22.300
You install it.

00:32:22.300 --> 00:32:23.100
You let it run.

00:32:23.100 --> 00:32:25.050
After that, you're pretty
much working on all your data

00:32:25.050 --> 00:32:27.000
and getting all of the
advanced deliverables

00:32:27.000 --> 00:32:28.650
that we can produce for you.

00:32:28.650 --> 00:32:31.920
So what I'd like to do is
talk a little bit for a second

00:32:31.920 --> 00:32:32.850
about security.

00:32:32.850 --> 00:32:34.740
It is a SaaS platform.

00:32:34.740 --> 00:32:39.330
All of the data we're collecting
is entirely metadata related.

00:32:39.330 --> 00:32:42.330
It's not application data,
not user data, nothing

00:32:42.330 --> 00:32:44.680
that falls under any
regulatory requirements.

00:32:44.680 --> 00:32:47.040
So there's no
issues around HIPAA

00:32:47.040 --> 00:32:48.690
or anything from
that perspective.

00:32:48.690 --> 00:32:50.820
And most importantly, we
have that conversation

00:32:50.820 --> 00:32:52.777
with your CSOs,
your security folks.

00:32:52.777 --> 00:32:54.360
If they want to ask
questions, there's

00:32:54.360 --> 00:32:56.250
a security white paper
that's available to them.

00:32:56.250 --> 00:32:57.720
Talks about every
field we collect.

00:32:57.720 --> 00:32:59.220
And what's really
neat is that they

00:32:59.220 --> 00:33:01.560
can inspect the actual
JSON files before they're

00:33:01.560 --> 00:33:03.047
transmitted into their portal.

00:33:03.047 --> 00:33:05.130
So you can see every single
field we're collecting

00:33:05.130 --> 00:33:07.200
and validate that what
we said we're collecting

00:33:07.200 --> 00:33:09.480
is what you're seeing
being transmitted.

00:33:09.480 --> 00:33:11.910
And everything's encrypted
in transit, encrypted

00:33:11.910 --> 00:33:14.160
at rest, all the usual things
that you would typically

00:33:14.160 --> 00:33:14.850
expect.

00:33:14.850 --> 00:33:16.770
But on top of all
of that, what we

00:33:16.770 --> 00:33:19.440
have is the ability
to custom anonymize.

00:33:19.440 --> 00:33:22.260
So if a specific customer says,
I don't want my IP addresses

00:33:22.260 --> 00:33:26.040
going into your cloud, your 192
is the same as my 192 range,

00:33:26.040 --> 00:33:28.565
but let's say you don't
want it in the cloud.

00:33:28.565 --> 00:33:30.690
You can actually select
the degree of anonymization

00:33:30.690 --> 00:33:32.680
that you'd like to
see in the platform.

00:33:32.680 --> 00:33:33.180
Right.

00:33:33.180 --> 00:33:34.980
So you can go all the
way to every piece

00:33:34.980 --> 00:33:36.760
of identifiable
data being removed

00:33:36.760 --> 00:33:38.760
or you can just have a
couple of things removed.

00:33:38.760 --> 00:33:41.760
Rarely happens, but the features
and capabilities are there.

00:33:44.550 --> 00:33:46.520
So last but not
least, once you've

00:33:46.520 --> 00:33:49.160
done all that great planning,
StratoZone as a platform

00:33:49.160 --> 00:33:50.540
goes from end to end.

00:33:50.540 --> 00:33:53.900
We're going to help you with
your business case, your data

00:33:53.900 --> 00:33:54.400
analysis.

00:33:54.400 --> 00:33:56.233
We're going to help you
put all of your plan

00:33:56.233 --> 00:33:57.340
together, build roadmaps.

00:33:57.340 --> 00:33:59.090
And we'll talk about
roadmaps in a second.

00:33:59.090 --> 00:34:01.160
Once you've built all
of that, you really

00:34:01.160 --> 00:34:03.320
need to leverage that
in your migration plan.

00:34:03.320 --> 00:34:06.560
One of the biggest
downfalls of migration plans

00:34:06.560 --> 00:34:09.525
is that a great plan was done,
but then the migration plan

00:34:09.525 --> 00:34:11.150
ends up being done
by a different team,

00:34:11.150 --> 00:34:13.108
different party, and it's
completely different.

00:34:13.108 --> 00:34:16.568
So here we actually carry all
of your planning and leverage

00:34:16.568 --> 00:34:18.110
your investment and
the previous work

00:34:18.110 --> 00:34:20.600
you did into the actual
migration process.

00:34:20.600 --> 00:34:23.060
And we integrate with
Velostrata for GCP.

00:34:23.060 --> 00:34:25.610
And it will automatically
build that runbook for you

00:34:25.610 --> 00:34:27.889
and actually move
the assets into GCP

00:34:27.889 --> 00:34:30.170
when you're looking at
doing a VM migration.

00:34:30.170 --> 00:34:32.721
So it's a very smooth process.

00:34:32.721 --> 00:34:34.429
You get a single pane
of glass to control

00:34:34.429 --> 00:34:36.020
your entire migration process.

00:34:36.020 --> 00:34:38.719
And what happens there is that
the business units that you

00:34:38.719 --> 00:34:41.719
work with are also,
at the end of the day,

00:34:41.719 --> 00:34:43.520
their process becomes smoother.

00:34:43.520 --> 00:34:45.887
And so they're more
likely to participate

00:34:45.887 --> 00:34:47.929
when you can show them
that you have an organized

00:34:47.929 --> 00:34:50.250
way of getting their assets
migrated into the cloud.

00:34:53.699 --> 00:34:57.630
Here's a quick example of
a process we went through.

00:34:57.630 --> 00:34:59.840
Our partner at
Maven Wave, customer

00:34:59.840 --> 00:35:03.530
eHarmony started data collection
of roughly 3,000 assets

00:35:03.530 --> 00:35:04.560
on a Friday.

00:35:04.560 --> 00:35:07.240
The whole business case was
ready presented on a Wednesday.

00:35:07.240 --> 00:35:07.740
Right.

00:35:07.740 --> 00:35:09.450
So you've got a lot
of analytics that

00:35:09.450 --> 00:35:10.740
go around the business case.

00:35:10.740 --> 00:35:13.080
And you can get to see
all of those details

00:35:13.080 --> 00:35:15.720
from dependency
mapping, the business

00:35:15.720 --> 00:35:18.690
case at the executive level,
the fully loaded TCO ROI.

00:35:18.690 --> 00:35:20.985
So it really is not
just a compute, storage,

00:35:20.985 --> 00:35:22.360
and memory kind
of business case.

00:35:22.360 --> 00:35:24.270
It is a fully loaded
business case including

00:35:24.270 --> 00:35:25.600
the cost of transition.

00:35:25.600 --> 00:35:27.630
And that's what the
platform will produce in

00:35:27.630 --> 00:35:30.330
literally 24 hours to three
days depending on how long you

00:35:30.330 --> 00:35:32.280
want to let the data run.

00:35:32.280 --> 00:35:34.780
So at this point, we're going
to jump into the platform real

00:35:34.780 --> 00:35:39.012
quick and do a demo.

00:35:39.012 --> 00:35:45.140
So StrataZone as a platform
is-- we'll reduce that size.

00:35:45.140 --> 00:35:47.110
There we go.

00:35:47.110 --> 00:35:48.340
It's a SaaS platform.

00:35:48.340 --> 00:35:51.130
What you see as a customer
is what your partners see.

00:35:51.130 --> 00:35:54.110
And it's also what your
deployment folks see.

00:35:54.110 --> 00:35:56.590
It is completely transparent.

00:35:56.590 --> 00:35:58.360
Pricing engine is
completely transparent.

00:35:58.360 --> 00:35:59.950
Everything's available to you.

00:35:59.950 --> 00:36:01.760
Kicking off an
assessment is very easy.

00:36:01.760 --> 00:36:03.880
It's basically a quick
form that you kick off

00:36:03.880 --> 00:36:05.140
once you get access.

00:36:05.140 --> 00:36:07.390
You do an automated
asset discovery.

00:36:07.390 --> 00:36:11.470
And all we need is who we're
going to email that one to.

00:36:11.470 --> 00:36:13.218
So assessments in general.

00:36:13.218 --> 00:36:15.010
You can have multiple
assessments globally.

00:36:15.010 --> 00:36:17.350
You can pull all
this data together.

00:36:17.350 --> 00:36:19.252
It does all of that
global sync for you,

00:36:19.252 --> 00:36:21.460
but we'd like to know where
your data is coming from.

00:36:21.460 --> 00:36:23.085
That's why you see
multiple assessments

00:36:23.085 --> 00:36:24.867
globally in multiple locations.

00:36:24.867 --> 00:36:26.450
Once you deploy those
data collectors,

00:36:26.450 --> 00:36:28.720
that's the end of any
work you do as a customer

00:36:28.720 --> 00:36:29.980
or as a partner.

00:36:29.980 --> 00:36:31.510
Everything comes
into the platform.

00:36:31.510 --> 00:36:32.590
It's maintained here.

00:36:32.590 --> 00:36:35.690
And you can sort and filter
through your different areas.

00:36:35.690 --> 00:36:37.357
But, most importantly,
what we're

00:36:37.357 --> 00:36:39.940
capturing-- this module, by the
way, runs entirely on its own.

00:36:39.940 --> 00:36:42.100
What we're capturing
for you is we're

00:36:42.100 --> 00:36:43.930
getting all of your
performance stats.

00:36:43.930 --> 00:36:45.250
We're profiling your assets.

00:36:45.250 --> 00:36:47.200
If you notice as
they come in, you'll

00:36:47.200 --> 00:36:49.510
see here you've got
all of your IOps

00:36:49.510 --> 00:36:51.970
and your performance
metrics, everything

00:36:51.970 --> 00:36:54.940
that's important to you
to do your right sizing

00:36:54.940 --> 00:36:55.820
and your pricing.

00:36:55.820 --> 00:36:57.403
And we'll talk about
that in a second.

00:36:57.403 --> 00:37:00.565
But our optimization engine
is extremely sophisticated.

00:37:00.565 --> 00:37:01.690
We call it the truth serum.

00:37:01.690 --> 00:37:03.050
A lot of our customers
will go to cloud

00:37:03.050 --> 00:37:05.383
and they'll come back and say
I used the TCO calculator.

00:37:05.383 --> 00:37:07.420
Cloud's more expensive
than my data center.

00:37:07.420 --> 00:37:08.878
Once they go through
this platform,

00:37:08.878 --> 00:37:10.253
we've challenged
every assumption

00:37:10.253 --> 00:37:12.160
and we've fed them very
realistic data center

00:37:12.160 --> 00:37:13.930
costs from our
benchmark data center

00:37:13.930 --> 00:37:16.780
and we can actually prove
a very, very solid business

00:37:16.780 --> 00:37:17.697
case around it.

00:37:17.697 --> 00:37:19.280
So, again, all your
data is coming in.

00:37:19.280 --> 00:37:21.580
All those things you see on
the left, the usual suspects,

00:37:21.580 --> 00:37:23.663
CPU utilization, memory
utilization, all of that's

00:37:23.663 --> 00:37:24.970
coming to the platform.

00:37:24.970 --> 00:37:26.537
We've processed
your dependencies.

00:37:26.537 --> 00:37:28.370
But, more importantly,
at this early stage--

00:37:28.370 --> 00:37:30.070
these are day two
reports by the way--

00:37:30.070 --> 00:37:32.260
at this early stage,
you can come in here

00:37:32.260 --> 00:37:34.570
and see what gets a high,
medium, and a low scoring

00:37:34.570 --> 00:37:35.530
for the cloud.

00:37:35.530 --> 00:37:37.400
And your first question
is going to be,

00:37:37.400 --> 00:37:39.275
well, why did I get a
high, medium, or a low.

00:37:39.275 --> 00:37:42.040
And it actually creates
your remediation plan

00:37:42.040 --> 00:37:45.430
and shows you with multiple
reasons like your credit report

00:37:45.430 --> 00:37:47.740
why you got a high,
medium, or low.

00:37:47.740 --> 00:37:50.350
So, if you look
through this process,

00:37:50.350 --> 00:37:53.320
every single thing has been
scored for you automatically.

00:37:53.320 --> 00:37:55.960
And you can actually give
the system some priorities

00:37:55.960 --> 00:37:57.320
and say this is important to me.

00:37:57.320 --> 00:37:58.605
That's not important to me.

00:37:58.605 --> 00:38:00.730
It's not important that
I'm able to exit the cloud,

00:38:00.730 --> 00:38:02.650
or I don't want my high
performance compute

00:38:02.650 --> 00:38:03.910
assets going to the cloud.

00:38:03.910 --> 00:38:06.470
So, once you do this, your
scoring actually changes.

00:38:06.470 --> 00:38:08.620
But the whole idea here is
based on your priorities

00:38:08.620 --> 00:38:12.130
we're giving you a very, very
solid machine based score that

00:38:12.130 --> 00:38:14.740
shows you, with the
underlying reasons,

00:38:14.740 --> 00:38:17.890
why you're a good fit for
the cloud or you're not.

00:38:17.890 --> 00:38:20.570
And, at this point, there's
lots of reports available.

00:38:20.570 --> 00:38:23.585
This is what we call
our day two reports.

00:38:23.585 --> 00:38:25.960
You've got all your detailed
reports that the data center

00:38:25.960 --> 00:38:26.620
folks would like.

00:38:26.620 --> 00:38:28.000
There's a bunch of
executive reports.

00:38:28.000 --> 00:38:29.560
But you can actually
come in here.

00:38:29.560 --> 00:38:31.300
The platform's
automatically right

00:38:31.300 --> 00:38:32.980
sized you and done
all the optimization.

00:38:32.980 --> 00:38:35.230
You can come in here, pick
your different locations,

00:38:35.230 --> 00:38:39.940
and generate a ROI calculation
right off the bat, basically

00:38:39.940 --> 00:38:41.770
an ROI, a savings calculation.

00:38:41.770 --> 00:38:44.230
And you can pick one or
more product catalogs

00:38:44.230 --> 00:38:45.490
that you want to see it from.

00:38:45.490 --> 00:38:47.830
Now, typically, we
make the other catalogs

00:38:47.830 --> 00:38:49.360
available in the
Google ecosystem.

00:38:49.360 --> 00:38:52.630
So you may want to actually
see what your comparative costs

00:38:52.630 --> 00:38:53.240
looks like.

00:38:53.240 --> 00:38:53.770
Right.

00:38:53.770 --> 00:38:55.660
But it's all real time catalogs.

00:38:55.660 --> 00:38:57.745
And they will present
you with the results

00:38:57.745 --> 00:38:59.620
that you can actually
take to your leadership

00:38:59.620 --> 00:39:01.468
and walk the cloud plan around.

00:39:01.468 --> 00:39:03.760
And to show you really quick
what that cloud plan looks

00:39:03.760 --> 00:39:08.170
like, it is going to
be a executive level

00:39:08.170 --> 00:39:09.648
presentation that
