00:39:24.670 --> 00:39:26.400
This is available
the next morning.

00:39:26.400 --> 00:39:27.082
Right.

00:39:27.082 --> 00:39:28.540
We'd like to have
24 hours of data.

00:39:28.540 --> 00:39:30.010
We can pull it in three
hours, but it's available

00:39:30.010 --> 00:39:30.860
next morning.

00:39:30.860 --> 00:39:32.290
So you've got a business case.

00:39:32.290 --> 00:39:34.330
You've got a very
solid determination.

00:39:34.330 --> 00:39:37.210
And this is based on
reality data underlying

00:39:37.210 --> 00:39:41.260
this, performance capacity,
and an actual real time catalog

00:39:41.260 --> 00:39:42.202
comparison.

00:39:42.202 --> 00:39:44.410
So, from here, I'd like to
show you a little bit more

00:39:44.410 --> 00:39:45.580
sophisticated functionality.

00:39:45.580 --> 00:39:47.320
We won't get too much on it.

00:39:47.320 --> 00:39:48.760
I've got four minutes left.

00:39:48.760 --> 00:39:50.530
So one of the big
things here, we

00:39:50.530 --> 00:39:52.990
have a very, very
sophisticated approach

00:39:52.990 --> 00:39:54.640
to doing machine shaping.

00:39:54.640 --> 00:39:58.780
And that is your paradigm
today of buying hardware

00:39:58.780 --> 00:40:03.700
and resourcing a data
center is based on capacity.

00:40:03.700 --> 00:40:07.150
The paradigm in the future
is based on elasticity.

00:40:07.150 --> 00:40:10.820
You've got the ability to scale
up and down as you see fit.

00:40:10.820 --> 00:40:14.090
So you need to change how
you're going to think.

00:40:14.090 --> 00:40:16.912
Again, speaking of the truth
serum, once we go through this,

00:40:16.912 --> 00:40:18.370
you're going to be
able to take out

00:40:18.370 --> 00:40:20.540
all of the inefficiency in
your current environment

00:40:20.540 --> 00:40:24.340
and then see what your real
cloud costs are going to be.

00:40:24.340 --> 00:40:28.120
That's really important, because
if you do a one to one match,

00:40:28.120 --> 00:40:30.370
you're simply taking your
inefficiency into the cloud.

00:40:30.370 --> 00:40:34.030
So this machine shaping
panel, we do it.

00:40:34.030 --> 00:40:36.688
A lot of the GCP ecosystem
partners will do it for you.

00:40:36.688 --> 00:40:38.230
But ultimately, it's
going to let you

00:40:38.230 --> 00:40:39.670
shape your life in the cloud.

00:40:39.670 --> 00:40:40.750
Very important.

00:40:40.750 --> 00:40:43.750
From here, you'll see that the
pricing engine will give you

00:40:43.750 --> 00:40:45.730
the ability to go
through and really do

00:40:45.730 --> 00:40:47.090
some skilled analysis.

00:40:47.090 --> 00:40:47.820
Right.

